<node id="Obstacles">
  <data key="d0">Obstacles</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Defensive measures employed by the stationary force commander to support the battle handover.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural or man-made features used to delay, disrupt, or destroy enemy forces and shape their movement.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural or man-made features identified by the intelligence process that restrict movement.&lt;SEP&gt;Defensive constructions planned and integrated into engagement areas to impede enemy movement.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural or reinforcing features used in engagement areas and defensive positions to disrupt enemy forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical barriers used by defending units to enhance the defensive strength of a position.&lt;SEP&gt;Obstacles are barriers that ground movement may encounter but air assaults can bypass.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-279aa3020dae92333d1d26e60241ff57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d54164de431a3e56787d0f04dea3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2039fcc410ab417ea95cf892f406c7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trafficability">
  <data key="d0">Trafficability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The capability of terrain to support the movement of vehicles or troops, identified through the intelligence process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-279aa3020dae92333d1d26e60241ff57</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cyberspace Operations">
  <data key="d0">Cyberspace Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Offensive or defensive operations in cyberspace that contribute to gaining and maintaining fire superiority.&lt;SEP&gt;Information-related capabilities synchronized to support the defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-279aa3020dae92333d1d26e60241ff57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d54164de431a3e56787d0f04dea3cf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Naval Surface Fire Support">
  <data key="d0">Naval Surface Fire Support</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Naval gunfire used as a joint fire to engage enemy forces throughout the depth of defensive positions.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of indirect fire used in aviation urban operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-279aa3020dae92333d1d26e60241ff57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a14acea44dac3d3616369b19ec0f2146</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Support">
  <data key="d0">Air Support</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Air power used as a joint fire to engage enemy forces throughout the depth of defensive positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-279aa3020dae92333d1d26e60241ff57</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fire Support Coordination Measures">
  <data key="d0">Fire Support Coordination Measures</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Measures used at each echelon to coordinate fires and prevent fratricide.&lt;SEP&gt;Measures used by commanders to control indirect fires, categorized into permissive and restrictive types.&lt;SEP&gt;Control measures employed by commanders to synchronize the employment of combat power and prevent fratricide.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-279aa3020dae92333d1d26e60241ff57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fratricide">
  <data key="d0">Fratricide</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The act of attacking friendly forces, prevented by proper coordination among fire cells and the use of FSCMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-279aa3020dae92333d1d26e60241ff57</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Harassing Fires">
  <data key="d0">Harassing Fires</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fires planned by the fire support coordinator to disturb the enemy's rest, curtail movement, and lower morale.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-279aa3020dae92333d1d26e60241ff57</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interdiction Fires">
  <data key="d0">Interdiction Fires</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fires planned by the fire support coordinator to disrupt enemy logistics and reinforcements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-279aa3020dae92333d1d26e60241ff57</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FLOT">
  <data key="d0">FLOT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A control measure that indicates the most forward positions of friendly forces in a military operation at a specific time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Limit Of Advance">
  <data key="d0">Limit Of Advance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A phase line used to control the forward progress of an attack, preventing elements from advancing beyond it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Objective">
  <data key="d0">Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A geographical feature or area that is the goal of a military operation.&lt;SEP&gt;A location used to orient operations, phase operations, facilitate changes of direction, and provide for unity of effort.&lt;SEP&gt;An objective is a designated location or feature that is the goal of an assault or military operation.&lt;SEP&gt;An area or object which a friendly force assaults and upon which direct fires are placed from a support by fire position.&lt;SEP&gt;A geographical area or object assigned to a force for seizure or destruction, often targeted by an attacking force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16d8c89f5caf99f0ea4f94711e809c9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64c2b09506eccedb4b06b038490a26a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac9465c9d545f87eb3a80e932a498f3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747313</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Line Of Contact">
  <data key="d0">Line Of Contact</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A general trace delineating the location where friendly and enemy forces are engaged.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Line Of Departure">
  <data key="d0">Line Of Departure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A line designated to coordinate the departure of attack elements and mark the transition from movement to maneuver.&lt;SEP&gt;A line crossed by the leading elements of the main body to initiate the attack.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64c2b09506eccedb4b06b038490a26a5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point Of Departure">
  <data key="d0">Point Of Departure</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The point where a unit crosses the line of departure and begins moving along a direction of attack.&lt;SEP&gt;The point crossed by leading elements in a limited-visibility attack to mark the time of attack.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64c2b09506eccedb4b06b038490a26a5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Probable Line Of Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Probable Line Of Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A phase line designating where a commander intends to deploy a unit into assault formation before beginning an assault.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rally Point">
  <data key="d0">Rally Point</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">An easily identifiable point on the ground at which units can reassemble and reorganize if they become dispersed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Objective Rally Point">
  <data key="d0">Objective Rally Point</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A rally point near an objective where infiltrating units assemble and prepare to attack.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Support By Fire Position">
  <data key="d0">Support By Fire Position</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A position from which a unit performs the tactical mission task of support by fire to increase the supported force's freedom of maneuver.&lt;SEP&gt;A general position from which a unit performs the tactical mission task of support by fire, normally located on the flank of the assault force and elevated above the objective.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64c2b09506eccedb4b06b038490a26a5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JP 3-03">
  <data key="d0">JP 3-03</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A publication referenced for the definition of the FLOT.&lt;SEP&gt;JP 3-03 is a joint publication referenced for information on joint interdiction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2039fcc410ab417ea95cf892f406c7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JP 3-31">
  <data key="d0">JP 3-31</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A publication referenced for the definition of the line of departure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ATP 3-21.20">
  <data key="d0">ATP 3-21.20</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A publication referenced for the definition of a rally point.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FEBA">
  <data key="d0">FEBA</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Acronym for Forward Edge of the Battle Area, referenced as a positional marker relative to the FLOT during defensive operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Forward Edge of the Battle Area, which serves as the forward boundary from which the Main Battle Area extends.&lt;SEP&gt;Forward Edge of the Battle Area, used as a reference for positioning echelon sustainment facilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e12f4d30fc2f3059510d3457b00e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSCM">
  <data key="d0">FSCM</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Acronym for Fire Support Coordination Measure, used to prevent friendly fire incidents for forces located forward of the FLOT.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Restrictive Fire Area">
  <data key="d0">Restrictive Fire Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific type of restrictive FSCM placed around friendly forces to prevent friendly fire incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific type of restrictive fire support coordination measure that may apply to friendly forces forward of the FLOT.&lt;SEP&gt;A restrictive fire support coordination measure where specific restrictions are applied.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phase Line">
  <data key="d0">Phase Line</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A control measure used to coordinate operations or control movement, such as the Limit of Advance or Probable Line of Deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;A line located on identifiable terrain used for control and coordination, such as designating a disengagement line.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direction Of Attack">
  <data key="d0">Direction Of Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The specific trajectory or route along which an attacking force advances toward an objective.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Assault Formation">
  <data key="d0">Assault Formation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A tactical configuration adopted by a unit to prepare for and initiate an assault.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infiltration">
  <data key="d0">Infiltration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A tactical movement method where forces conduct operations through enemy positions, often utilizing rally points.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Assault Position">
  <data key="d0">Assault Position</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">An assault position is a covered and concealed position short of the objective where final preparations are made to assault the objective.&lt;SEP&gt;A covered and concealed position short of the objective used for final preparations to assault the objective.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16d8c89f5caf99f0ea4f94711e809c9b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Final Coordination Line">
  <data key="d0">Final Coordination Line</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A phase line close to the enemy position used to coordinate the lifting or shifting of supporting fires with the final deployment of maneuver elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Assault Time">
  <data key="d0">Assault Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The moment designated to attack the initial objectives throughout the geographical scope of the operation, imposed by a higher echelon headquarters to achieve simultaneous results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Higher Echelon Headquarters">
  <data key="d0">Higher Echelon Headquarters</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A command element that imposes timing and establishes criteria for subordinate units.&lt;SEP&gt;The command structure above the current unit that establishes air defense priorities.&lt;SEP&gt;The headquarters that directs when and where to conduct a relief and establishes control measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71131e902d37087dc65113f52eae4eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b036aa74f3adbdabd1d826936e991c47</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747906</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Field Artillery">
  <data key="d0">Field Artillery</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military branch that uses the time on target control method for fire mission processing.&lt;SEP&gt;A military unit utilizing indirect fire weapons to quickly engage enemy forces in landing and drop zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attack by Fire Position">
  <data key="d0">Attack by Fire Position</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A general position from which a unit performs the tactical task of attack by fire to mass the effects of direct fire systems on the enemy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy">
  <data key="d0">Enemy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The opposing force or hostile entity in a military operation.&lt;SEP&gt;The opposing force that may detect operations, particularly simultaneous relief in place.&lt;SEP&gt;An adversary force or entity about which reconnaissance aims to obtain information regarding activities and resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversary forces whose use of subsurface areas can be observed, disrupted, or destroyed.&lt;SEP&gt;Opposing forces that may provide early warning, emplace obstacles, or engage aircraft from structures in the urban environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The opposing force whose cohesion, situational awareness, and logistics are targeted to reduce ability to mass combat power.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a88d8c8678543b9eb4fa95b4ea87591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b036aa74f3adbdabd1d826936e991c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfe3e79800d49e6c15cc7d1d7485cab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d765189e92be25ee08b9a34a1f6fb186&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bdc5217db0cca10554a11bb5c365968</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778758129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attack Position">
  <data key="d0">Attack Position</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The last position an attacking force occupies or passes through before crossing the line of departure, offering cover and concealment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Line of Departure">
  <data key="d0">Line of Departure</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A line that an attacking force crosses to initiate an offensive operation.&lt;SEP&gt;A line at which a unit crosses to begin an operation, serving as the starting point for an area reconnaissance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a88d8c8678543b9eb4fa95b4ea87591</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747904</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axis of Advance">
  <data key="d0">Axis of Advance</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The general area through which the bulk of a unit's combat power must move.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bypass Criteria">
  <data key="d0">Bypass Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Measures established by higher echelon headquarters specifying the conditions and size under which enemy units and contact may be avoided.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battle Handover Line">
  <data key="d0">Battle Handover Line</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A designated phase line where responsibility transitions from a stationary force to a moving force and vice versa.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stationary Force">
  <data key="d0">Stationary Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military force that remains in a defensive position while responsibility is transitioned to a moving force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Moving Force">
  <data key="d0">Moving Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military force that advances and accepts responsibility from a stationary force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Forward Edge of the Battle Area">
  <data key="d0">Forward Edge of the Battle Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The foremost limits of the areas occupied by the main battle forces on the battlefield.&lt;SEP&gt;A designated line or area established during operations in depth to define the front of the main battle area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Forward Line of Own Troops">
  <data key="d0">Forward Line of Own Troops</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A line indicating the most forward positions of friendly forces in a military operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direction of Attack">
  <data key="d0">Direction of Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific direction or assigned route a force uses and does not deviate from when attacking, maximizing control over movement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point of Departure">
  <data key="d0">Point of Departure</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific point designated on a line of departure where a unit crosses to begin an attack.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Engineers">
  <data key="d0">Engineers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Personnel who perform final prepare-to-fire checks on obstacle clearing systems during assault preparations.&lt;SEP&gt;Engineers are the principal staff integrators for the assured mobility framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8e712cfc21b1d5eeb7e94fcc0ac1db7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crews">
  <data key="d0">Crews</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Personnel operating plow- or roller-equipped tanks who remove locking pins during final preparations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Obstacle Clearing Systems">
  <data key="d0">Obstacle Clearing Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Technical systems checked by engineers to ensure they are ready for firing during final preparations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tanks">
  <data key="d0">Tanks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Armored vehicles, specifically those equipped with plows or rollers, used by crews during assault preparations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Probable Line of Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Probable Line of Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A line near which an assault position may be located.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time of Attack">
  <data key="d0">Time of Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A timing concept used by commanders instead of assault time when distances and obstacles vary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contaminated Areas">
  <data key="d0">Contaminated Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Hazardous locations that can delay an advancing force and are subject to bypass criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Forces">
  <data key="d0">Security Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Units employed by the stationary force commander in the area between the battle handover line and the stationary force.&lt;SEP&gt;Units that prevent the enemy from discerning friendly dispositions or interfering with attack preparations.&lt;SEP&gt;Forces operating in areas excluded from the Forward Edge of the Battle Area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6bf6abab46637a933d4adcc9ec578f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fires">
  <data key="d0">Fires</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Fires refer to the use of weapon systems to create lethal or non-lethal effects, supporting attacks and operations in depth.&lt;SEP&gt;The use of weapon systems employed by the stationary force commander in the area near the battle handover line.&lt;SEP&gt;Fires are used to neutralize, suppress, destroy, delay, or disrupt enemy forces and enhance the effects of massed direct fires.&lt;SEP&gt;Potential events affecting thermal-imagery, night-vision devices, and health of personnel.&lt;SEP&gt;Military fires that must be used judiciously until the IP is located and require coordination between ground and airborne forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Fires are used by enemy forces in proximity to their locations to cause thermal washout effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16d8c89f5caf99f0ea4f94711e809c9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b14fece49276b354d02ce9679408699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-410889a9720065d35de43976293caee3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ff2850046e68e7092903c98bb6595e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751488</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Target Reference Points">
  <data key="d0">Target Reference Points</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific points used as a means to establish a direction of attack.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific type of direct fire control measure used to control engagement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Checkpoints">
  <data key="d0">Checkpoints</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific points used as a means to establish a direction of attack.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fire Support Coordination Measure">
  <data key="d0">Fire Support Coordination Measure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A measure or restriction used to coordinate fire support; the final coordination line is explicitly not one of these.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reconnaissance Assets">
  <data key="d0">Reconnaissance Assets</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Small, long-range units to which the forward line of own troops does not apply.&lt;SEP&gt;Resources oriented by commanders towards a reconnaissance objective within an area of operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a88d8c8678543b9eb4fa95b4ea87591</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747904</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stay-Behind Forces">
  <data key="d0">Stay-Behind Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Forces similar to reconnaissance assets to which the forward line of own troops does not apply.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Covering Forces">
  <data key="d0">Covering Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Forces whose forward location is normally identified by the forward line of own troops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Screening Forces">
  <data key="d0">Screening Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Forces whose forward location is normally identified by the forward line of own troops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Armored BCT">
  <data key="d0">Armored BCT</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Armored Brigade Combat Teams require careful planning and allocation of organic mobility capabilities to maintain offensive momentum.&lt;SEP&gt;Armored Brigade Combat Team, requires careful planning and allocation of mobility capabilities to maintain offensive momentum.&lt;SEP&gt;Armored Brigade Combat Team, a type of Army BCT capable of conducting security operations and tactical marches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8e712cfc21b1d5eeb7e94fcc0ac1db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ce33eb77548e57e227d14350711715</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747905</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stryker BCT">
  <data key="d0">Stryker BCT</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Stryker Brigade Combat Teams require careful planning and allocation of organic mobility capabilities to maintain offensive momentum.&lt;SEP&gt;Stryker Brigade Combat Team, requires careful planning and allocation of mobility capabilities to maintain offensive momentum.&lt;SEP&gt;Stryker Brigade Combat Team, a type of Army BCT capable of conducting security operations and tactical marches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8e712cfc21b1d5eeb7e94fcc0ac1db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ce33eb77548e57e227d14350711715</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747906</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hasty Breach">
  <data key="d0">Hasty Breach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A hasty breach, also known as an in-stride breach, is the preferred method for defeating a defended obstacle to avoid loss of time and momentum.&lt;SEP&gt;An in-stride method of defeating a defended obstacle preferred to avoid the loss of time and momentum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8e712cfc21b1d5eeb7e94fcc0ac1db7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deliberate Breach">
  <data key="d0">Deliberate Breach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of breach that involves planning, resourcing, and execution, often associated with a loss of time and momentum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wet Gap">
  <data key="d0">Wet Gap</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A major obstacle such as a river that requires complex combined arms operations to cross.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dry Gap">
  <data key="d0">Dry Gap</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A major obstacle such as an anti-vehicular ditch that hinders military movement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gap Crossing">
  <data key="d0">Gap Crossing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Gap crossing is a primary mobility task included in mobility operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A complex operation conducted by maneuver units to traverse wet or dry gaps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8e712cfc21b1d5eeb7e94fcc0ac1db7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hasty Crossing">
  <data key="d0">Hasty Crossing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of gap crossing conducted as a continuation of the attack to avoid giving the enemy time to strengthen defenses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clearing Operations">
  <data key="d0">Clearing Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Operations designed to clear or neutralize mines and obstacles from a route or area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Countermobility">
  <data key="d0">Countermobility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combined arms activities using obstacles to deny enemy freedom of movement and maneuver.&lt;SEP&gt;Countermobility is a task category integrated within the assured mobility framework alongside mobility and protection.&lt;SEP&gt;A focus area for engineers during the transition to defense, prioritized over mobility.&lt;SEP&gt;Countermobility involves the use of obstacles to impede enemy movement and maneuver, complementing defensive operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8e712cfc21b1d5eeb7e94fcc0ac1db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tank Ditches">
  <data key="d0">Tank Ditches</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Man-made obstacles constructed to deny enemy mobility corridors and protect flanks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abatis">
  <data key="d0">Abatis</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Man-made obstacles used to deny enemy mobility corridors and provide flank security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road Craters">
  <data key="d0">Road Craters</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Man-made obstacles created to deny enemy mobility corridors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Engineer">
  <data key="d0">Engineer</data>
