</node>
<node id="Reconnaissance Units">
  <data key="d0">Reconnaissance Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Units used to maintain contact and surveillance of enemy forces during transitions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surveillance Assets">
  <data key="d0">Surveillance Assets</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Assets used in combination with reconnaissance units to develop information required for planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Area">
  <data key="d0">Security Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A designated zone established to enhance security during the transition to defensive operations.&lt;SEP&gt;An area established by commanders in the defense to provide protection and reduce unknowns.&lt;SEP&gt;An area occupied by security elements to provide early warning and protection to the main force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Force">
  <data key="d0">Security Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A force established to provide security, supported by redeployed artillery assets.&lt;SEP&gt;A military unit tasked with conducting security operations, such as delaying the enemy to buy time for the main body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adjacent Units">
  <data key="d0">Adjacent Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Neighboring units with which a force maintains or regains contact in a contiguous Area of Operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Area of Operations">
  <data key="d0">Area of Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The geographical area assigned to a unit for conducting military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;An area assigned to a commander, distinct from a battle position, carrying specific doctrinal responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The area within which a commander identifies a reconnaissance objective.&lt;SEP&gt;The Army term for the assigned zone of operations where responsibilities are transferred during a relief in place.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a88d8c8678543b9eb4fa95b4ea87591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b036aa74f3adbdabd1d826936e991c47</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sustainment Effort">
  <data key="d0">Sustainment Effort</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The logistical support system that shifts focus from moving forward to ensuring the ability to defend.&lt;SEP&gt;Logistical support activities that shift focus depending on the operation, such as fuel for offense or supplies for defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac9465c9d545f87eb3a80e932a498f3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747313</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Petroleum, Oils, and Lubricants">
  <data key="d0">Petroleum, Oils, and Lubricants</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplies resupplied to ensure a force's ability to move forward during offensive operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Casualty Evacuation">
  <data key="d0">Casualty Evacuation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The process of moving injured personnel, facilitated by a reduction in tempo during transition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778745999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hasty Defense">
  <data key="d0">Hasty Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A defensive posture established without deliberate preparation, often characterized by time and resource constraints.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrograde">
  <data key="d0">Retrograde</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An operation conducted when a commander determines it is necessary to stop an offensive operation.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of military operation where a force not in contact with an enemy moves to another location, including delays, withdrawals, and retirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrograde is a type of defensive operation involving organized movement away from the enemy, performed voluntarily or under compulsion to regain the initiative.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of movement operation that can involve a passage of lines.&lt;SEP&gt;A planned movement for a friendly force during reconnaissance in force if it encounters superior enemy forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef422907967635431abf4581ffee5bb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a88d8c8678543b9eb4fa95b4ea87591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b036aa74f3adbdabd1d826936e991c47</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747904</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Area Defense">
  <data key="d0">Area Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A defensive operation conducted by subordinate units from current locations during a retrograde.&lt;SEP&gt;Area Defense is a type of defensive operation that focuses on denying enemy forces access to designated terrain for a specific time rather than destroying the enemy outright.&lt;SEP&gt;A defensive method where units use engagement areas to concentrate combat power from mutually supporting positions.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of defense where commanders designate a portion of the force to conduct a counterattack.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac9465c9d545f87eb3a80e932a498f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef422907967635431abf4581ffee5bb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1cd0ab6021273635c13e3b7af3476</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Campaign Plan">
  <data key="d0">Campaign Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A strategic plan that defines phases and sequels for major operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Civil Institutions">
  <data key="d0">Civil Institutions</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Existing organizations within an area that coordinate with military forces and NGOs during stability operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nongovernmental Organizations">
  <data key="d0">Nongovernmental Organizations</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Entities that coordinate with military forces to address stability concerns and provide essential services.&lt;SEP&gt;Nongovernmental Organizations are entities with which Army special operations forces develop enduring partnerships.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-950f5d02c8283b123e3471016b2f74a1</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778758118</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Civilian Inhabitants">
  <data key="d0">Civilian Inhabitants</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The population within an Area of Operations requiring essential services like food, water, and shelter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legitimacy of the Mission">
  <data key="d0">Legitimacy of the Mission</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The validity of the mission which faces significant risk during the transition to stability operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operational Force">
  <data key="d0">Operational Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A force configuration that is reconfigured into an occupation force during transition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Occupation Force">
  <data key="d0">Occupation Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A force configuration established after reconfiguring from an operational force to provide security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Threats">
  <data key="d0">Threats</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversarial entities that seek to establish networks to circumvent the security environment and prolong transition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Safe Havens">
  <data key="d0">Safe Havens</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Secure locations that friendly forces seek to deny to threats during the transition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="End State">
  <data key="d0">End State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The desired final condition that commanders actively seek to achieve while consolidating gains.&lt;SEP&gt;The desired final situation that the commander's intent describes, providing subordinates with a clear goal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d54164de431a3e56787d0f04dea3cf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Resources">
  <data key="d0">Combat Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Materials and assets belonging to former enemies that friendly forces must account for.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Major Operation">
  <data key="d0">Major Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A large-scale military undertaking where stability operations may serve as the decisive phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Psychological Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Psychological Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The mental shift required for soldiers to transition from an offensive to a defensive mindset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Constraints">
  <data key="d0">Resource Constraints</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Severe limitations on time and assets that characterize hasty defensive preparations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Losses">
  <data key="d0">Combat Losses</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Personnel or equipment losses incurred during combat that are replaced by the sustainment effort.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="The Offense">
  <data key="d0">The Offense</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The decisive form of war and the ultimate means commanders have of imposing their will on enemy forces, characterized by audacity, concentration, surprise, and tempo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audacity">
  <data key="d0">Audacity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A characteristic of the offense defined as a willingness to take bold risks and act decisively to seize the initiative.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A characteristic of the offense involving the massing of combat power effects in time and space at the decisive point.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746000</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surprise">
  <data key="d0">Surprise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A characteristic of the offense achieved by attacking at an unexpected time, place, or manner to delay enemy reactions and induce psychological shock.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operation Desert Storm">
  <data key="d0">Operation Desert Storm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A historical military operation where a turning movement was executed against the Iraqi Republican Guard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VII Corps">
  <data key="d0">VII Corps</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit that executed a turning movement into the flank and rear of the Iraqi Republican Guard during Operation Desert Storm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XVIII Corps">
  <data key="d0">XVIII Corps</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit that executed a turning movement into the flank and rear of the Iraqi Republican Guard during Operation Desert Storm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iraqi Republican Guard">
  <data key="d0">Iraqi Republican Guard</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The enemy force targeted by VII and XVIII Corps during the turning movement in Operation Desert Storm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terrain">
  <data key="d0">Terrain</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Terrain is a physical objective that commanders seek to control or use to achieve a position of relative advantage.&lt;SEP&gt;The physical landscape studied by defending forces to improve defensive positions.&lt;SEP&gt;The physical environment occupied and prepared by defending forces to gain advantages over attackers.&lt;SEP&gt;A component of urban areas that ASCOPE aligns with.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d54164de431a3e56787d0f04dea3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef422907967635431abf4581ffee5bb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d765189e92be25ee08b9a34a1f6fb186</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751492</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resources">
  <data key="d0">Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resources are assets that commanders aim to gain control of or deprive the enemy of during offensive operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778746001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Population Centers">
  <data key="d0">Population Centers</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Population centers are key locations that commanders seek to gain control of during the offense.&lt;SEP&gt;Population centers may be bypassed by forces during large-scale combat operations advancement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69d05b2f34d86a1867e7e7939634802</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778758129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decisive Point">
  <data key="d0">Decisive Point</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The decisive point is the specific location in time and space where combat power is massed to achieve a single purpose.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific point in time or space where a commander can gain a significant advantage, often the focus of defensive control measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Information Systems">
  <data key="d0">Information Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Information systems provide relevant information that helps commanders determine when to concentrate their forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Systems used by commanders to accurately tailor combat-configured loads to the demands of supported maneuver units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e12f4d30fc2f3059510d3457b00e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unified Action Partner">
  <data key="d0">Unified Action Partner</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unified action partners are entities whose capabilities are coordinated in multiple domains to create opportunities for offensive land operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Partner whose activities are integrated with intelligence operations to enhance situational awareness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a75fd9bf2d8ffd7deb7994794314ba94</data>
