  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weapons of Mass Destruction">
  <data key="d0">Weapons of Mass Destruction</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Weapons of Mass Destruction are employed by enemy forces to greatly increase casualties and the burden on medical resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Weapons that pose a significant risk of large-scale losses to concentrated forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Destructive agents or weapons whose potential employment triggers survivability moves to protect forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Weapons of Mass Destruction are cited as a threat complicating rear area protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Weapons of mass destruction are among the threats that rear area security forces must counter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71131e902d37087dc65113f52eae4eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1cd0ab6021273635c13e3b7af3476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d90513532ac94b30a700a8204e509e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69d05b2f34d86a1867e7e7939634802</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778758124</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Service Support">
  <data key="d0">Health Service Support</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Health Service Support is a component of sustainment responsible for medical care and evacuation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71131e902d37087dc65113f52eae4eb8</data>
