</node>
<node id="Commanders">
  <data key="d0">Commanders</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Commanders are military leaders responsible for directing unit operations, guiding the actions of subordinates, and making critical decisions to defeat or destroy enemy forces. As central decision-makers, they play a pivotal role in conducting offensive operations to seize the initiative, creating dilemmas for adversaries, and designating decisive terrain. They shape the battlefield by employing security forces, positioning combat multipliers, and accepting risk to mass effects at decisive points. Their leadership extends to building effective teams through professional development, visualizing complex operational environments, and making tactical decisions regarding unit deployment, engagement, force repositioning, and economy of force measures.

In the realm of planning and execution, commanders develop mission orders, establish control measures, and determine objectives to direct tactical actions. They are responsible for synchronizing capabilities, planning transitions between defensive, offensive, and stability operations, and issuing orders to subordinate units. This involves detailed oversight of movement formations, the concentration of combat power, and considerations regarding soldier load. Specifically regarding fire support, they visualize the synchronization of fires, place Fire Support Coordination Measures (FSCMs), and coordinate fire effects to disrupt enemy forces, while also assessing preparation fires and determining munitions usage.

Furthermore, commanders oversee defensive and specialized operational functions to ensure force resilience. They plan denial operations, establish support priorities, and synchronize protection capabilities, integrating countermobility and survivability tasks. This includes allocating resources, coordinating movements, and directing defensive operations. They leverage intelligence products to visualize the battlefield, direct information operations, and establish air defense priorities. Additionally, they ensure units can conduct decontamination, integrate reconnaissance, and plan for population and resource control. Through these diverse responsibilities, commanders serve as the central figures who synchronize combat power and direct the overall military effort.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who direct enabling operations and orient reconnaissance assets to support offensive, defensive, and stability operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who establish priorities for movement control and coordinate responsibilities during operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaders responsible for identifying building characteristics and understanding weapon effects within the area of operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Military leaders who should keep in mind objectives regarding the civilian populace and consider societal implications.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaders responsible for planning and executing operations, emphasizing unified planning and standards in urban topology.&lt;SEP&gt;Commanders are military personnel granted access to the IPPS-A system for managing personnel and pay data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fe75aaa5c3fd7e0ce8f1c7accd42b83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e273c9c49d54aea292dd6741d10a78d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-279aa3020dae92333d1d26e60241ff57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c73d56d8e9bfb3038d769d096b30c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da551c8c73e884b03192b52010d81be5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4240b292090a3a425c9dae95b6a7c26a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8e712cfc21b1d5eeb7e94fcc0ac1db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b45e15d5cccdd3d631ceeba2a6d8d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6bf6abab46637a933d4adcc9ec578f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abe3f08fafe8b7389e20d639ffaa8692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa0cb96393bbc79e8f283b9593a9806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71131e902d37087dc65113f52eae4eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a418b78a90bc5acb3f47736189745955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e12f4d30fc2f3059510d3457b00e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fea48c62cf850e8a658d6027f583efe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef422907967635431abf4581ffee5bb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1cd0ab6021273635c13e3b7af3476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a88d8c8678543b9eb4fa95b4ea87591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b036aa74f3adbdabd1d826936e991c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d765189e92be25ee08b9a34a1f6fb186&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-446c344294ac1157381c690e0f0b5d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb60400466a6008ca4dd586ce73558f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503de8a915400d2e62dbb9df698d826a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\WEAPON_SYSTEMS_HANDBOOK.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778831622</data>
