  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retirement">
  <data key="d0">Retirement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A movement where a force out of contact moves away from the enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;Retirement is a variation of retrograde mentioned alongside delay and withdrawal as a type of defensive operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef422907967635431abf4581ffee5bb8</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battle Position">
  <data key="d0">Battle Position</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A defensive location oriented on a likely enemy avenue of approach, used by units ranging from squads to battalion task forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Battle positions are defensive locations that achieve maximum mutual support when located to observe ground or conduct patrols to prevent enemy infiltration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Primary Position">
  <data key="d0">Primary Position</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The position covering the enemy's most likely avenue of approach, considered the best location to accomplish the defensive mission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alternate Position">
  <data key="d0">Alternate Position</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A defensive position assigned for occupation when the primary position becomes untenable, allowing occupants to fulfill the original task.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supplementary Position">
  <data key="d0">Supplementary Position</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A defensive position located within an area of operations to cover sectors of fire along an avenue of approach that is not the primary avenue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subsequent Position">
  <data key="d0">Subsequent Position</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A position that a unit expects to move to during the course of battle, which may have its own primary, alternate, and supplementary positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strong Point">
  <data key="d0">Strong Point</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A heavily fortified battle position tied to a natural or reinforcing obstacle to create an anchor for the defense or deny the enemy key terrain.&lt;SEP&gt;A defensive position requiring significant time, resources, and engineer support to construct, typically occupied by companies or battalions to secure a perimeter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Avenue of Approach">
  <data key="d0">Avenue of Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A route or path likely used by enemy forces to advance into an area of operations, influencing the orientation of battle positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disengagement Line">
  <data key="d0">Disengagement Line</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A control measure designated by commanders to trigger the displacement of subordinate forces.&lt;SEP&gt;A phase line on identifiable terrain that signals defending elements to displace to their next position when crossed by the enemy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Engagement Area">
  <data key="d0">Engagement Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">An area where the commander intends to contain and destroy an enemy force with the massed effects of all available weapons.&lt;SEP&gt;A designated area where the commander intends to contain and destroy an enemy force using available weapons systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A designated area where defending forces initiate combat on favorable terms against enemy forces.&lt;SEP&gt;A geographical area where integrating obstacles with fires is intended to halt or slow enemy movement and destroy the enemy force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Fire Control">
  <data key="d0">Direct Fire Control</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A control measure used by commanders to distribute and direct the fires of weapons systems against enemy targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fighting Position">
  <data key="d0">Fighting Position</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A prepared location within a battle position providing protection and a platform for weapons systems, vehicles, and Soldiers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Engineer Unit">
  <data key="d0">Engineer Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit responsible for constructing defensive positions like strong points.&lt;SEP&gt;A military unit responsible for constructing fortifications, such as strong points and battle positions.&lt;SEP&gt;Military units responsible for performing mobility tasks such as breaching obstacles, clearing routes, and maintaining combat roads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defense">
  <data key="d0">Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of military operations that is usually stronger than the offense, conducted to create conditions favorable for the offense or to counter enemy action.&lt;SEP&gt;A military operation characterized by a mix of static and dynamic actions designed to defeat an enemy attack.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of military operation where a force withstands enemy action, potentially transitioning to the offense or retrograde operations based on success.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac9465c9d545f87eb3a80e932a498f3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Main Battle Area">
  <data key="d0">Main Battle Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The area where the commander intends to deploy the bulk of the unit's combat power and conduct decisive operations to defeat an attacking enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;An area established by commanders during operations in depth, associated with the Forward Edge of the Battle Area.&lt;SEP&gt;The area extending from the Forward Edge of the Battle Area to the rear boundary, where the defending force engages the enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;The primary area where defensive forces engage the enemy, often involving static roles for dismounted infantry.&lt;SEP&gt;The area where a defending force is less effective if an attacking enemy force can deploy in combat formations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Main Battle Area, referred to as MBA, is a location where commanders position survivability positions and conducting defensive operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fea48c62cf850e8a658d6027f583efe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1cd0ab6021273635c13e3b7af3476</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defending Force">
  <data key="d0">Defending Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The military unit conducting defensive operations, employing field fortifications and obstacles.&lt;SEP&gt;A military organization that conducts operations in multiple domains to disrupt enemy plans, degrade capabilities, and regain the initiative.&lt;SEP&gt;A defending force employs indirect and joint fires to engage enemy forces and operates within the Main Battle Area (MBA).&lt;SEP&gt;A military unit tasked with protecting areas, containing enemy forces, and conducting counterattacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1cd0ab6021273635c13e3b7af3476</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IPB Process">
  <data key="d0">IPB Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intelligence Preparation of the Battlefield, a method used to analyze the terrain and anticipate enemy actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Intelligence Preparation of the Battlefield, a process used to determine enemy capabilities, such as vertical envelopment, and identify potential drop and landing zones.&lt;SEP&gt;A process that utilizes information from reconnaissance to formulate, confirm, or modify courses of action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a88d8c8678543b9eb4fa95b4ea87591</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Avenue Of Approach">
  <data key="d0">Avenue Of Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A route or path used by an enemy force to reach its objective, analyzed during the IPB process.&lt;SEP&gt;A route or path used by forces to move towards an objective, which can be impeded by obstacles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Operations">
  <data key="d0">Security Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Operations conducted to provide time and space for the main force to react, including delay and disruption of the enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations performed to protect forces and assets, deter or defeat enemy reconnaissance, and create standoff distances.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations that orient on the force or facility being protected to prevent surprise and reduce unknowns, serving as shaping operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e12f4d30fc2f3059510d3457b00e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ce33eb77548e57e227d14350711715</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747904</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Field Fortifications">
  <data key="d0">Field Fortifications</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Structures constructed by defending forces to improve the survivability of their units.&lt;SEP&gt;Defensive structures employed by defending units to reinforce the terrain's natural defensive aspects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef422907967635431abf4581ffee5bb8</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserve">
  <data key="d0">Reserve</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Reserve encompasses two distinct interpretations within military frameworks: a tactical doctrinal element and a specific organizational component. In the context of tactics, Reserve denotes a designated force element retained by commanders separate from the main engagement. This portion of the military force is held back to exploit opportunities, regain superiority, or preserve defense integrity. Commanders employ this body of troops to reinforce fires, add depth, block enemy advances, or restore a position. Depending on the situation, such as when the enemy force is too large or preparation time is limited, the size of the Reserve may increase. During shaping operations, a defending commander commits and reconstitutes these forces. They serve to mass effects, counterattack enemy successes, or reinforce threatened positions. These forces are available to conduct offensive operations with higher readiness after being held back from initial contact.

Separately, Reserve identifies a component of the United States military involved in logistics and modernization. In this capacity, the entity is integrated into Army modernization efforts where it receives fielded ESP HEMTT vehicles. Furthermore, as a component of the United States military, it acquires fielded PLSA1 vehicles through the Extended Service Program. While the tactical definition focuses on operational maneuver and force preservation, the organizational description highlights specific equipment integration. Together, these descriptions illustrate the multifaceted nature of the Reserve in maintaining both immediate battlefield capabilities and long-term technological readiness within the armed forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adabd6aa6271efdc850feccf7016cdf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a418b78a90bc5acb3f47736189745955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d54164de431a3e56787d0f04dea3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef422907967635431abf4581ffee5bb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1cd0ab6021273635c13e3b7af3476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1c7260e4a898eeeb86c6568add6249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef40d1e9a5996f2179f1b53a42ee90d</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\WEAPON_SYSTEMS_HANDBOOK.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778831675</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Class I">
  <data key="d0">Class I</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of supplies including water for CBRN decontamination and consumption, required for constructing battle positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Class IV">
  <data key="d0">Class IV</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of supplies consisting of construction materials required for building battle positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Class V">
  <data key="d0">Class V</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of supplies consisting of ammunition required for battle positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Final Protective Fire">
  <data key="d0">Final Protective Fire</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An immediately available, prearranged barrier of fire designed to impede enemy movement across defensive lines or areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Forward Edge Of The Battle Area">
  <data key="d0">Forward Edge Of The Battle Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The foremost limits of a series of areas where ground combat units are deployed, marking the planned limit for direct fire effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Forward Line Of Own Troops">
  <data key="d0">Forward Line Of Own Troops</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A line indicating the most forward positions of friendly forces in any kind of military operation at a specific time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Fire Control Measures">
  <data key="d0">Direct Fire Control Measures</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Measures used by commanders to control fires, including target reference points and trigger lines.&lt;SEP&gt;Measures established by headquarters to control direct fire during linkup operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac9465c9d545f87eb3a80e932a498f3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trigger Lines">
  <data key="d0">Trigger Lines</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific type of direct fire control measure used to control engagement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Company">
  <data key="d0">Company</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit size that normally occupies strong points.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battalion">
  <data key="d0">Battalion</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit size that normally occupies strong points.&lt;SEP&gt;A military unit echelon for which defending an AO is a typical mission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d54164de431a3e56787d0f04dea3cf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brigade">
  <data key="d0">Brigade</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit size that may construct strong points.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Platoon">
  <data key="d0">Platoon</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit size considered too small to secure a perimeter for a strong point.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Squad">
  <data key="d0">Squad</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit size considered too small to secure a perimeter for a strong point.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Coordinated Fire Line">
  <data key="d0">Coordinated Fire Line</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A permissive fire support coordination measure used to control indirect fires.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSCLs">
  <data key="d0">FSCLs</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Fire Support Coordination Lines, identified as a type of permissive fire support coordination measure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Free-Fire Area">
  <data key="d0">Free-Fire Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A permissive fire support coordination measure where weapons may be fired without coordination.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airspace Coordination Area">
  <data key="d0">Airspace Coordination Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A restrictive fire support coordination measure used to coordinate airspace usage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="No Fire Area">
  <data key="d0">No Fire Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A restrictive fire support coordination measure where fires are prohibited.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747295</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Friendly Fire Incidents">
  <data key="d0">Friendly Fire Incidents</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Unintentional firing on friendly forces, which restrictive fire support coordination measures aim to prevent.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk increased by unique characteristics of shantytowns such as narrow pathways and weapon penetration.&lt;SEP&gt;Friendly fire incidents are critical to prevent through positive identification of friendly positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16fb9a43ba23b08191569577e00618b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32189ba42b4061e42fcfd89b6143133c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-446c344294ac1157381c690e0f0b5d6c</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MBA">
  <data key="d0">MBA</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Main Battle Area where enemy forces attempt to break through defending units.&lt;SEP&gt;The MBA, or Main Battle Area, is the location where a defending force is less effective if an attacking enemy force deploys there.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d54164de431a3e56787d0f04dea3cf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indirect and Joint Fires">
  <data key="d0">Indirect and Joint Fires</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Indirect and joint fires are employed by a defending force to attack enemy forces in vulnerable locations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fire Support Chain">
  <data key="d0">Fire Support Chain</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The fire support chain includes observers and cells that must understand the commander's intent to execute the scheme of maneuver.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSCMs">
  <data key="d0">FSCMs</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fire Support Coordination Measures are placed by commanders to enable the rapid engagement of attacking enemy forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Fire Support Coordination Measures established by headquarters to control fire support during linkup operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac9465c9d545f87eb3a80e932a498f3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fire Support Assets">
  <data key="d0">Fire Support Assets</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Fire support assets target enemy combat units to force deployment, inflict casualties, and disrupt the cohesion of attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FPFs">
  <data key="d0">FPFs</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Final Protective Fires are priority targets designated for artillery units and mortar platoons during defensive operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Artillery Units">
  <data key="d0">Artillery Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Artillery units are supporting units that can be assigned a single FPF and are laid on targets when not engaged in other missions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mortar Platoons">
  <data key="d0">Mortar Platoons</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Mortar platoons are supporting units designated to conduct defensive operations and assigned FPFs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Army Air Defense Artillery Forces">
  <data key="d0">Army Air Defense Artillery Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Army air defense artillery forces operate interdependently to provide air and missile defense and protect high-value assets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aerial Threats">
  <data key="d0">Aerial Threats</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Aerial threats are enemy dangers that air defense artillery forces aim to deter or defeat to protect the force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Force Commander">
  <data key="d0">Joint Force Commander</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Joint Force Commander seeks to gain and maintain air superiority to allow friendly forces to operate without prohibitive interference.&lt;SEP&gt;The Joint Force Commander receives working knowledge of critical infrastructure from Army special operations forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3a0c67aeaade5d9ae17a53e58e80e73</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778758131</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Superiority">
  <data key="d0">Air Superiority</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Air superiority is a condition required by the Joint Force Commander to ensure freedom of operation for friendly forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ground Commanders">
  <data key="d0">Ground Commanders</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ground commanders mitigate the risk of air and missile attack through various activities to improve unit survivability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Camouflage">
  <data key="d0">Camouflage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Camouflage is an activity used by ground commanders to reduce the likelihood of detection from the air.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ammunition">
  <data key="d0">Ammunition</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ammunition is a priority item for replenishment in the defensive plan and may be stockpiled within the MBA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Denial Operations">
  <data key="d0">Denial Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Denial operations involve plans to destroy stockpiled ammunition and supplies if necessary during a defense.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations where commanders plan to destroy stocks if necessary to prevent enemy use.&lt;SEP&gt;Operations conducted by designated units during retrograde movements to delay or disrupt enemy forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e12f4d30fc2f3059510d3457b00e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac9465c9d545f87eb3a80e932a498f3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Obstacle Plan">
  <data key="d0">Obstacle Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Obstacle Plan is a tactical plan that the fire support chain must understand to distribute fire effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High-Payoff Targets">
  <data key="d0">High-Payoff Targets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High-Payoff Targets are specific targets that friendly forces aim to destroy or neutralize without wasting assets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Fire Systems">
  <data key="d0">Direct Fire Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct Fire Systems are weapons that engage enemy forces canalized by obstacles and fire support coverage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Final Protective Line">
  <data key="d0">Final Protective Line</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A Final Protective Line is a predetermined line assigned to a direct fire weapon system as a form of Final Protective Fires.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High-Value Assets">
  <data key="d0">High-Value Assets</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">High-Value Assets are critical resources protected by Army air defense artillery forces during operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early Warning">
  <data key="d0">Early Warning</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Early Warning is information disseminated to units to improve survivability by predicting impact points and detecting launches.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerts provided to a protected force regarding enemy activity, the primary output of screen operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ce33eb77548e57e227d14350711715</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747905</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sustainment Unit Commanders">
  <data key="d0">Sustainment Unit Commanders</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Commanders who understand the supported commander’s intent and establish support priorities for sustainment operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Sustainment Unit Commanders understand the supported commander's intent and establish support priorities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d61f4b5597bdee4add1bccdba2cbd3ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e12f4d30fc2f3059510d3457b00e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drop Zone">
  <data key="d0">Drop Zone</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific area identified by the IPB process where enemy forces are expected to parachute personnel or supplies.&lt;SEP&gt;A designated area where troops or supplies are dropped by parachute, subject to risk prioritization and surveillance by commanders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Landing Zone">
  <data key="d0">Landing Zone</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific area identified by the IPB process where enemy forces are expected to land aircraft for air assault operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A designated area where aircraft can land, subject to risk prioritization, surveillance, and targeting by defending forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Offensive Counterair Support">
  <data key="d0">Joint Offensive Counterair Support</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of support that commanders may request to counter enemy air threats offensively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defensive Counterair Support">
  <data key="d0">Defensive Counterair Support</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of support that commanders may request to defend against enemy air threats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy Insertion">
  <data key="d0">Enemy Insertion</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The act of enemy forces placing troops or equipment into an area, which defending forces attempt to detect and counter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fire Support Plan">
  <data key="d0">Fire Support Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A plan that includes target lists for drop and landing zones to cover potential enemy insertion areas.&lt;SEP&gt;A plan that includes drop and landing zones in its target list for area fires and scatterable munitions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Area Fires Munitions">
  <data key="d0">Area Fires Munitions</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Munitions included in the fire support plan to target specific zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scatterable Munitions">
  <data key="d0">Scatterable Munitions</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Munitions deployed over a wide area, included in the fire support plan for drop and landing zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Friendly Installation">
  <data key="d0">Critical Friendly Installation</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Key facilities or sites that defending forces protect through countermobility and survivability efforts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attack Helicopter">
  <data key="d0">Attack Helicopter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An armed aircraft used to quickly engage enemy forces concentrated in landing and drop zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Fires">
  <data key="d0">Joint Fires</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fires employed against enemy insertion areas using assets from two or more components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Base Cluster Defense">
  <data key="d0">Base Cluster Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A defensive force responsible for keeping enemy forces under observation and designating targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quick Response Force">
  <data key="d0">Quick Response Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A rapidly deployable unit that fixes enemy forces to allow a tactical combat force to counterattack.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Combat Force">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Combat Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A unit committed to counterattack enemy forces that have landed and consolidated.&lt;SEP&gt;A tactical combat force is a unit that responds to Level III threats after military police maintain contact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Sight">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Sight</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A mechanical aid capable of overcoming or partially overcoming darkness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Target Acquisition Optic">
  <data key="d0">Target Acquisition Optic</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Devices used by enemy forces for targeting, the use of which can be denied by obscurants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligence Officer">
  <data key="d0">Intelligence Officer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A staff member who coordinates the development of a synchronized information collection plan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Information Collection Plan">
  <data key="d0">Information Collection Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A synchronized and integrated plan developed to satisfy maneuver, targeting, and information requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The information collection plan is the overall strategy into which commanders integrate CBRN reconnaissance and surveillance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligence Product">
  <data key="d0">Intelligence Product</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis used by commanders to identify probable enemy objectives, approaches, and vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Named Area Of Interest">
  <data key="d0">Named Area Of Interest</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific area identified by commanders during planning to focus intelligence collection efforts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Targeted Area Of Interest">
  <data key="d0">Targeted Area Of Interest</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific area identified by commanders, often developed from probable enemy objectives and approaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IPB">
  <data key="d0">IPB</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intelligence Preparation of the Battlefield, a process used to determine enemy strength, courses of action, and vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy Follow-on Force">
  <data key="d0">Enemy Follow-on Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Reinforcement units that arrive after the initial enemy assault, whose location and commitment time are analyzed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Information Collection Asset">
  <data key="d0">Information Collection Asset</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Resources used to gather intelligence, which require sustainment and protection due to susceptibility to loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Army Indirect Fire">
  <data key="d0">Army Indirect Fire</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fires delivered by Army assets not in direct line of sight of the target, used to neutralize or destroy enemy forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Response Force">
  <data key="d0">Response Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A military unit that, along with base cluster defense, keeps enemy forces under observation and designates targets for available fires.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mechanical Aid">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Aid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Equipment such as thermal sights that can overcome or partially overcome limited visibility conditions like darkness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Darkness">
  <data key="d0">Darkness</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A limited visibility condition that mechanical aids can overcome or partially overcome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Devices that may retain value in limited visibility conditions where mechanical aids are ineffective.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Staff">
  <data key="d0">Staff</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Personnel who support commanders by rapidly transmitting coordination decisions to all concerned.&lt;SEP&gt;The group with whom intelligence officers coordinate to develop a synchronized information collection plan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d54164de431a3e56787d0f04dea3cf</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cyberspace Activity">
  <data key="d0">Cyberspace Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Operations in cyberspace identified by IPB products regarding enemy forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Avenue Of Approach">
  <data key="d0">Air Avenue Of Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A route through the airspace used by forces, which obscurants can deny the enemy from using.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visual Navigation Aid">
  <data key="d0">Visual Navigation Aid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tools used for navigation that obscurants can deny an enemy force from using.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Observation">
  <data key="d0">Observation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A military aspect of terrain that commanders determine to assess visibility and fields of view.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Field Of Fire">
  <data key="d0">Field Of Fire</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A military aspect of terrain referring to the area a weapon can cover effectively, determined by commanders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cover And Concealment">
  <data key="d0">Cover And Concealment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A military aspect of terrain used for protection from enemy observation and fire, determined by commanders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defensive Plan">
  <data key="d0">Defensive Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A plan that must address the sustainment, replacement, and reconstitution of information collection assets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-069de81fea4e6c37c85bab0a5a971f89</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attack Using Uncommitted Forces">
  <data key="d0">Attack Using Uncommitted Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The preferred method for transitioning to the offense using forces from the reserve or reinforcements not previously committed to defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a418b78a90bc5acb3f47736189745955</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reinforcements">
  <data key="d0">Reinforcements</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Additional military forces that arrive to support operations, capable of conducting attacks without prior combat fatigue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a418b78a90bc5acb3f47736189745955</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attack Using Defending Forces">
  <data key="d0">Attack Using Defending Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method for transitioning to the offense using forces currently engaged in defense, offering speed and surprise.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a418b78a90bc5acb3f47736189745955</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Negotiated End To Hostilities">
  <data key="d0">Negotiated End To Hostilities</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A diplomatic resolution that may trigger a transition from defensive operations to stability operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a418b78a90bc5acb3f47736189745955</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Units In Contact">
  <data key="d0">Units In Contact</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Military forces currently engaged with the enemy that must be retained to fix enemy forces during an attack.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a418b78a90bc5acb3f47736189745955</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subordinate Units">
  <data key="d0">Subordinate Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Military units under a commander's control that are reinforced to execute an attack or maintain defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a418b78a90bc5acb3f47736189745955</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserve Assembly Areas">
  <data key="d0">Reserve Assembly Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Locations where reserve forces gather, requiring an approach or tactical road march to reach the front lines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a418b78a90bc5acb3f47736189745955</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AOs">
  <data key="d0">AOs</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Areas of Operation prepared by defending units before attacking enemy forces arrive or established behind a security force.&lt;SEP&gt;Areas of Operations from which reinforcements may move to join the engagement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a418b78a90bc5acb3f47736189745955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef422907967635431abf4581ffee5bb8</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CBRN Hazards">
  <data key="d0">CBRN Hazards</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CBRN hazards are threats analyzed using Mission-oriented protective posture analysis to determine appropriate protective measures.&lt;SEP&gt;CBRN hazards are threats from chemical, biological, radiological, and nuclear sources against which defending units are vulnerable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fea48c62cf850e8a658d6027f583efe1</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission-oriented Protective Posture">
  <data key="d0">Mission-oriented Protective Posture</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mission-oriented protective posture (MOPP) is a method used to determine protective posture and estimate unit effectiveness against hazards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MOPP Analysis">
  <data key="d0">MOPP Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MOPP analysis is a tool used to determine appropriate protective posture and estimate logistic requirements during CBRN threats.&lt;SEP&gt;MOPP analysis is a tool used to support determining protective posture, estimating logistic requirements, and assessing tradeoffs between agent exposure and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fea48c62cf850e8a658d6027f583efe1</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CBRN Personnel">
  <data key="d0">CBRN Personnel</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">CBRN personnel contribute to unit protection, perform vulnerability assessments, and recommend vulnerability reduction measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CBRN Vulnerability Assessment">
  <data key="d0">CBRN Vulnerability Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CBRN vulnerability assessments include threat assessment and vulnerability analysis to provide preventive measures for CBRN defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Security">
  <data key="d0">Physical Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical security is an operation that commanders prioritize throughout a defense, especially during noncontiguous operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antiterrorism">
  <data key="d0">Antiterrorism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antiterrorism involves operations that commanders monitor throughout a defense to protect against enemy attacks indistinguishable from terrorist acts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Military Police Elements">
  <data key="d0">Military Police Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Military police elements support defending units by enhancing physical security and antiterrorism capabilities within an echelon support area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Level II Threats">
  <data key="d0">Level II Threats</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Level II threats are security risks that military police may defeat against bases and base clusters located in an echelon support area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Level III Threats">
  <data key="d0">Level III Threats</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Level III threats are security risks that military police maintain contact with until a tactical combat force responds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Population And Resource Control">
  <data key="d0">Population And Resource Control</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Population and resource control measures are planned by commanders to manage dislocated civilians and minimize effects on the defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dislocated Civilians">
  <data key="d0">Dislocated Civilians</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dislocated civilians are populations that affect the defense and are managed using host-nation and international organizations to minimize disaster effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Civil Affairs Units">
  <data key="d0">Civil Affairs Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Civil affairs units assist commanders in planning population and resource control measures during defensive operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil Affairs Units conduct operations to leverage civilian capabilities and support partner government recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil Affairs Units work with civilian authorities and Army protection units to reestablish civil control, essential services, and coordinate populace and resources control measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Partner with critical civil networks to rapidly reconstitute partner governance capacity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d90513532ac94b30a700a8204e509e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bdc5217db0cca10554a11bb5c365968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660d19754e7a8b4d28766ae683085446</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778758122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breakout">
  <data key="d0">Breakout</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A breakout is an operation conducted by an encircled force to regain freedom of movement or contact with friendly units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Encircled Force">
  <data key="d0">Encircled Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">An encircled force is a military unit surrounded by enemy forces, often conducting a breakout or exfiltration to survive.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exfiltration">
  <data key="d0">Exfiltration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Exfiltration is an organized method to preserve a portion of a force if a breakout fails or is questionable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seizure Of Key Terrain">
  <data key="d0">Seizure Of Key Terrain</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Seizure of key terrain is a risky course of action where an encircled force attacks deeper into enemy territory.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy Supply Stocks">
  <data key="d0">Enemy Supply Stocks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Enemy supply stocks are resources that an isolated unit may use to sustain itself while attacking deeper.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linkup">
  <data key="d0">Linkup</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A linkup is a meeting of friendly ground forces occurring in various circumstances, such as after a breakout.&lt;SEP&gt;A meeting of friendly ground forces occurring in various circumstances, such as when an advancing force reaches an objective or an encircled element breaks out.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac9465c9d545f87eb3a80e932a498f3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Friendly Ground Forces">
  <data key="d0">Friendly Ground Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Friendly ground forces are military units that meet during a linkup operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Military units that conduct linkups, advance on objectives, or engage in defensive and offensive operations against enemy forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac9465c9d545f87eb3a80e932a498f3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Personnel">
  <data key="d0">Medical Personnel</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical personnel continuously maintain and conduct comprehensive health surveillance including medical, occupational, and environmental aspects.&lt;SEP&gt;Trained individuals who advise the commander on whether to use MEDEVAC and CASEVAC.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfe3e79800d49e6c15cc7d1d7485cab2</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751444</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Surveillance">
  <data key="d0">Health Surveillance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Health surveillance is a comprehensive activity conducted by medical personnel to monitor health and environmental conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CBRN Passive Defense Training">
  <data key="d0">CBRN Passive Defense Training</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CBRN passive defense training is a responsibility of commanders to prepare units to respond properly to CBRN threats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conventional Reconnaissance Assets">
  <data key="d0">Conventional Reconnaissance Assets</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Conventional reconnaissance assets are existing capabilities whose efforts should not be duplicated by CBRN reconnaissance and surveillance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vulnerability Reduction Measures">
  <data key="d0">Vulnerability Reduction Measures</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Vulnerability reduction measures are recommendations provided by CBRN personnel to commanders to enhance protection before and after moving into defensive positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Civilian Population Centers">
  <data key="d0">Civilian Population Centers</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Civilian population centers are locations attacked by enemy forces in an attempt to disrupt the defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Support Area">
  <data key="d0">Support Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">An area where terrain management is critical for establishing bases and base clusters.&lt;SEP&gt;The support area is a zone that must be protected from enemy attacks to ensure the success of a unit defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e12f4d30fc2f3059510d3457b00e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="International Organizations">
  <data key="d0">International Organizations</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">International organizations are entities used by defending units to minimize the effects of disaster or conflict on dislocated civilians.&lt;SEP&gt;International Organizations are entities with which Army special operations forces develop enduring partnerships.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-950f5d02c8283b123e3471016b2f74a1</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778758118</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perimeter">
  <data key="d0">Perimeter</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The perimeter is the area where an encircled force must maintain a simultaneous defense during a breakout operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy Rear Area">
  <data key="d0">Enemy Rear Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The enemy rear area is a location where an encircled friendly force may attack to disrupt the enemy's offense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d85f7f19b9f147f37bc741a7c59d700</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disruption">
  <data key="d0">Disruption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A characteristic of the defense involving actions to desynchronize enemy preparations, isolate forward echelons, and target command and control systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flexibility">
  <data key="d0">Flexibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A characteristic of the defense requiring plans that anticipate enemy actions and allow for shifting the main effort and allocating resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maneuver">
  <data key="d0">Maneuver</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A characteristic of the defense that allows a force to achieve and exploit a position of advantage using static and mobile elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mass and Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Mass and Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A characteristic of the defense involving the production of overwhelming combat power at specific locations to support decisive operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operations in Depth">
  <data key="d0">Operations in Depth</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The simultaneous application of combat power throughout an area of operations to disrupt enemy capabilities and prevent early successes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preparation">
  <data key="d0">Preparation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A characteristic of the defense involving the occupation and improvement of positions, study of terrain, and preparation of engagement areas before contact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security">
  <data key="d0">Security</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A characteristic of the defense utilizing security forces to protect defending forces from surprise and reduce unknowns.&lt;SEP&gt;An enabling operation discussed in the context of military actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a88d8c8678543b9eb4fa95b4ea87591</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combined Arms">
  <data key="d0">Combined Arms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The synchronization of different military arms, which disruption actions aim to impede.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Command and Control Systems">
  <data key="d0">Command and Control Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Enemy systems targeted by defending forces to disrupt operations in depth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Engagement Areas">
  <data key="d0">Engagement Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Engagement Areas are designated locations where defending forces combine obstacles and fires to destroy or canalize enemy forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Specific areas prepared by defending forces to intercept and engage the enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;Designated zones where defending forces integrate direct and indirect fires to defeat enemy attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Designated locations where units concentrate fires to destroy or degrade the enemy in an area defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12d54164de431a3e56787d0f04dea3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef422907967635431abf4581ffee5bb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1cd0ab6021273635c13e3b7af3476</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defending Forces">
  <data key="d0">Defending Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Defending Forces are units that prepare their areas of operation before enemy forces arrive, establishing defenses, studying terrain, and preparing engagement areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The specific military units conducting defensive operations, improving positions, and maneuvering against the enemy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3345760dcbfb2262ee6ddfa43b1677ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef422907967635431abf4581ffee5bb8</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mutual Support">
  <data key="d0">Mutual Support</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mutual support exists when positions and units support each other by direct and indirect fires, preventing enemy forces from attacking one position without being subjected to fire from adjacent positions.&lt;SEP&gt;A tactical condition where positions support each other by direct and indirect fires to strengthen defenses and prevent infiltration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1cd0ab6021273635c13e3b7af3476</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reinforcing Obstacle">
  <data key="d0">Reinforcing Obstacle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Artificial obstacles constructed or emplaced to augment existing natural obstacles, categorized as either tactical or protective.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Obstacle">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Obstacle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of reinforcing obstacle designed to shape enemy maneuver, maximize the effects of fires, and affect the tempo of operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Protective Obstacle">
  <data key="d0">Protective Obstacle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of reinforcing obstacle employed to protect personnel, equipment, supplies, and facilities against threats in defensive or security roles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserved Obstacle">
  <data key="d0">Reserved Obstacle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific obstacle for which the commander retains execution authority to allow coordination with other battlefield activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fire">
  <data key="d0">Fire</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The use of weapon systems to create lethal effects, integrated with obstacles to enhance their effectiveness and canalize enemy movement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy Airborne and Air Assault Attack">
  <data key="d0">Enemy Airborne and Air Assault Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An offensive operation involving enemy forces utilizing vertical envelopment via drop zones or landing zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertical Envelopment">
  <data key="d0">Vertical Envelopment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A maneuver tactic where enemy forces bypass defensive lines by air, using drop zones or landing zones to insert troops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unit Leader">
  <data key="d0">Unit Leader</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A leader responsible for coordinating the nature and extent of mutual support within a defensive position.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-832f2104ac2a57f71576e95a87a29163</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778747306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scatterable Mine">
  <data key="d0">Scatterable Mine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of mine with specific firing and self-destruct times used to create obstacles.</data>
