</node>
<node id="Joint Operating Environment 2035">
  <data key="d0">Joint Operating Environment 2035</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Joint Operating Environment 2035 is a source document stating that humanity is becoming a predominantly urban species.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urban Terrain">
  <data key="d0">Urban Terrain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Urban Terrain is a component of the urban environment consisting of airspace, supersurface, surface, and subsurface categories.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airspace">
  <data key="d0">Airspace</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Airspace is a category of urban terrain that may be congested due to civilian air traffic and unmanned aircraft systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supersurface">
  <data key="d0">Supersurface</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Supersurface is the area above ground level consisting of man-made structures like buildings and towers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surface">
  <data key="d0">Surface</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Surface is the category of urban terrain at ground level including streets, alleys, and parks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subsurface">
  <data key="d0">Subsurface</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Subsurface is the area below ground level consisting of sewers, tunnels, and utility corridors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small Unmanned Aircraft Systems">
  <data key="d0">Small Unmanned Aircraft Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Small Unmanned Aircraft Systems are emerging aviation technology employed in urban airspace by various users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Terminal Attack Controllers">
  <data key="d0">Joint Terminal Attack Controllers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Joint Terminal Attack Controllers are ground personnel who must understand communication restrictions caused by the supersurface.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
