  <data key="d5">1778751459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Army Techniques Publication 3-21.51">
  <data key="d0">Army Techniques Publication 3-21.51</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Army Techniques Publication 3-21.51 provides information on subterranean operations and the subsurface environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Publication 3-06">
  <data key="d0">Joint Publication 3-06</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Joint Publication 3-06 states objectives regarding the civilian populace in joint urban operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Document titled Joint Urban Operations stating objectives regarding the civilian populace for commanders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d765189e92be25ee08b9a34a1f6fb186</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Civilian Populace">
  <data key="d0">Civilian Populace</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Civilian Populace lives in cities and military operations aim to minimize interference with them.&lt;SEP&gt;The population of an urban area considered as a center of gravity requiring legal, moral, and humanitarian obligations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d765189e92be25ee08b9a34a1f6fb186</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Society">
  <data key="d0">Society</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Society is one of the three components of urban environments alongside terrain and supporting infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supporting Infrastructure">
  <data key="d0">Supporting Infrastructure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Supporting Infrastructure is a component of urban environments that varies from one urban area to another.&lt;SEP&gt;Vital parts of infrastructure that can be destroyed, controlled, or protected to isolate a threat but may have unintended consequences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d765189e92be25ee08b9a34a1f6fb186</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Host Nation">
  <data key="d0">Host Nation</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Host Nation operates the air traffic control system within which urban-area airspace may be congested.&lt;SEP&gt;The nation whose security threats are addressed by partner resilience activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d264de22c88d1296cd175906c25ab76b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778758120</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Air Assets">
  <data key="d0">Air Assets</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Military units that observe, disrupt, or destroy the enemy's use of subsurface areas based on ground force identification.&lt;SEP&gt;Air Assets can observe, disrupt, or destroy the enemy's use of subsurface areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d765189e92be25ee08b9a34a1f6fb186</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urban Canyons">
  <data key="d0">Urban Canyons</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Urban Canyons are contained within the supersurface and can cause weapons delivery restrictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Urban Canyons are specific features of the urban environment that increase effects on low altitude flight and complicate sensor tasking.&lt;SEP&gt;Urban Canyons are vertical structures in urban environments that present challenges for weapon trajectories and aircraft attack headings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2039fcc410ab417ea95cf892f406c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94b0f13f75f0bd64d503a14651482e66</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Infrastructure">
  <data key="d0">Critical Infrastructure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical Infrastructure includes building foundations, power lines, gas lines, and water lines that must be considered prior to weapons employment.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure can be damaged or degraded by friendly backed partner forces to disrupt enemy sustainment.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical Infrastructure is essential to preserving relative advantage and may be sabotaged by special operations forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure includes facilities and essential services that Army special operations forces provide working knowledge of.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d90513532ac94b30a700a8204e509e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69d05b2f34d86a1867e7e7939634802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3a0c67aeaade5d9ae17a53e58e80e73</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778758125</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commercial Users">
  <data key="d0">Commercial Users</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Commercial Users employ emerging aviation technology in the airspace with no direct involvement in the conflict.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c503bd64404512328ab83ccc0ba0997e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
