<node id="Aircrews">
  <data key="d0">Aircrews</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Aircrews are personnel responsible for operating aviation assets and planning and executing aircraft operations, including the development of alternate extraction methods. Their operational scope requires a thorough understanding of theater evacuation policy and strict adherence to avoiding overflight of urban terrain. When navigating these environments, aircrews must consider obstacle clearance and line of sight geometry while managing limited engagement times in urban settings. They face specific environmental challenges, such as cultural lighting that can degrade Night Vision Devices, necessitating careful visual identification of friendly positions.

During missions, aircrews utilize Ground Moving Target Indicator (GMTI) systems for focused area searches and must independently determine resolutions for Positive Identification (PID), Collateral Damage (CD), and Rules of Engagement (ROE) during air interdiction. A critical aspect of their decision-making process involves considering the secondary effects of striking targets and potential collateral damage. To maintain safety and effectiveness, aircrews coordinate with Joint Terminal Attack Controllers (JTACs) and rely on Suppression of Enemy Air Defenses (SEAD) fire for protection. Through these combined technical, tactical, and planning responsibilities, aircrews ensure the successful execution of aviation assets within complex operational theaters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfe3e79800d49e6c15cc7d1d7485cab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a14acea44dac3d3616369b19ec0f2146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8dbf8d99e2395e386c1df16f3ddc745&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2039fcc410ab417ea95cf892f406c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32189ba42b4061e42fcfd89b6143133c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39bd2e6c05ba9ec2683ab1b01bd4603d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02c0ca8e3a28d2a5576fbc54974744ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb60400466a6008ca4dd586ce73558f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ff2850046e68e7092903c98bb6595e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778751477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
