<node id="Detroit Arsenal">
  <data key="d0">Detroit Arsenal</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Detroit Arsenal is a facility located in Michigan that operates as a significant base for various United States Army Program Executive Offices. It is primarily identified as the operational location and base hosting PEO Ground Combat Systems, which holds responsibility for the Advanced Mobile Protected Firepower Vehicle (AMPV) program. Throughout its operation, the Arsenal has served consistently as the physical location associated with this executive office within the state.

Additionally, Detroit Arsenal functions as the facility housing PEO Combat Support and Combat Service Support. This association links the location to a diverse array of defense logistics and equipment contracts, including automotive transaction agreements. Under this specific executive support, the Arsenal is connected to the High Mobility Multipurpose Wheeled Vehicle (HMMWV) program and manages Mine Resistant Ambush Protected (MRAP) vehicle acquisition and sustainment efforts. Furthermore, the site supports the PLS Extended Service Program, cementing its role in sustaining combat support and service support capabilities across multiple vehicle platforms and logistical frameworks in Michigan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-663e6d2263b508d6a68885919457bd03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acade8ec9a9d5344060a4314cfa18a5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd09d5c1d391b2d64517a5d72254efc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc1b95a684a1e8d5c4b01db867ca78af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dcb0d8a5efb5ce308ca2c93988c72be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3473302fed80b78e94b810b62c26e3a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a37387a27a64b26277551e337553582b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15fb7baa23082d86c7d6fc25d3cc0e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-193261eb3b1bd80c929ecfd74166b738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f976415bdf294d82666a68528ec01480</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\WEAPON_SYSTEMS_HANDBOOK.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778831578</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soldier Lethality">
  <data key="d0">Soldier Lethality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Soldier Lethality is a designated strategic modernization priority of the United States Army. It functions as one of the six modernization priorities identified by the Army for long-range improvement and holds a specific designation as a TACA Modernization Priority within the United States Army acquisition strategy. This priority area is central to the Army's efforts regarding individual soldier capabilities and overall force enhancement.

The core objective of Soldier Lethality focuses on enhancing the combat effectiveness, lethality, and survivability of the individual soldier and warfighter. While primarily targeting individual combat capability, firepower, and protection, the initiative also encompasses soldiers and their platforms. Specific elements of this modernization include improvements such as Stryker lethality upgrades and the provision of networking tactical radio systems to warfighters. Through these combined measures, the program aims to deliver comprehensive improvements to the individual warfighter's operational readiness and protective systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-663e6d2263b508d6a68885919457bd03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acade8ec9a9d5344060a4314cfa18a5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd09d5c1d391b2d64517a5d72254efc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c4507fc3a4f571c8dfbaa23d9a738cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e07adaae816a485b8bdcdde27baecf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d02d8715ba139ee7e2b9f2ae7c7d9bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e04593a83987ff6eb98f28906bbd37f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a15c71581af907f47533c1630b8096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dcb0d8a5efb5ce308ca2c93988c72be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6faa94aab2e13591315f79ebbd49ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3473302fed80b78e94b810b62c26e3a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15fb7baa23082d86c7d6fc25d3cc0e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7ca33dacb79b2456dfa0debe68053e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-278d433e3502ea4bdab16646b23bed0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d121313ed4af44c28824fd63c5a94377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adaee111f19e7fd13f315f0ca1141b82</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\WEAPON_SYSTEMS_HANDBOOK.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778831586</data>
