<node id="United States Army">
  <data key="d0">United States Army</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The United States Army serves as the primary military branch operating armored and aviation assets, functioning as the overarching organization for acquisition, deployment, and sustainment of described weapon systems. It utilizes the Abrams tank as its primary ground combat system and oversees programs such as the Armored Multi-Purpose Vehicle (AMPV) and Integrated Air and Missile Defense (IAMd). The branch sets modernization priorities including Future Vertical Lift, Long-Range Precision Fires, Soldier Lethality, and the Army Network, managing projects from Acquisition Life Cycle phases to fleet lethality enhancements.

Operational capabilities encompass a wide range of vehicles and systems. Ground mobility involves the Family of Medium Tactical Vehicles (FMTV), Stryker program for rapid deployability, High Mobility Multipurpose Wheeled Vehicles (HMMWV), Heavy Expanded Mobility Tactical Trucks (HEMTT), the PLSA1 fleet, and Utility Helicopter (UH-72A) for homeland defense. Protection and recovery are ensured through Mine Resistant Ambush Protected (MRAP) vehicles and the M88A2 Improved Recovery Vehicle. Combat firepower includes the High Mobility Artillery Rocket System (HIMARS), Multiple Launch Rocket System (MLRS), Paladin, M109A7 Self-Propelled Howitzer, and Guided Multiple Launch Rocket System (GMLRS). Missiles operated or procured include the Javelin, Joint Air-to-Ground Missile (JAGM), TOW, and Excalibur Projectile. Air assets involve helicopters and the MQ-1C Gray Eagle drone.

Technical infrastructure supports these operations through the Distributed Common Ground System-Army (DCGS-A) for intelligence and sensor tasking, alongside networking tactical radio systems. Administrative and logistical management relies on the General Fund Enterprise Business System (GFEBS) and Integrated Personnel and Pay System-Army (IPPS-A). The United States Army holds milestone authority for the Phased Array Tracking Radar and Intercept System (PAC-3) and operates the PATRIOT system, ensuring continuous implementation of upgrades to operational forces across all described domains.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-663e6d2263b508d6a68885919457bd03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acade8ec9a9d5344060a4314cfa18a5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd09d5c1d391b2d64517a5d72254efc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65ec4365c5ad1d3448d3d2041d7edb2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc1b95a684a1e8d5c4b01db867ca78af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c4507fc3a4f571c8dfbaa23d9a738cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e07adaae816a485b8bdcdde27baecf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d02d8715ba139ee7e2b9f2ae7c7d9bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2c67ada43a04708429aa1e720d42cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e04593a83987ff6eb98f28906bbd37f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a15c71581af907f47533c1630b8096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb3d0930de98ddce6ed3ada6a6c40cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4b4ce335843ab582068db841084575c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503de8a915400d2e62dbb9df698d826a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e0c57d3e73a6d0c3b1cbe5a2f59e546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dcb0d8a5efb5ce308ca2c93988c72be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6faa94aab2e13591315f79ebbd49ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3473302fed80b78e94b810b62c26e3a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a37387a27a64b26277551e337553582b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15fb7baa23082d86c7d6fc25d3cc0e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7ca33dacb79b2456dfa0debe68053e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-278d433e3502ea4bdab16646b23bed0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-193261eb3b1bd80c929ecfd74166b738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d121313ed4af44c28824fd63c5a94377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f976415bdf294d82666a68528ec01480&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1c7260e4a898eeeb86c6568add6249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed783d4ec3a234cf3d010d793d561f17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef40d1e9a5996f2179f1b53a42ee90d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e097e89b46e0363b0e3141cd6e6f7d1</data>
