  <data key="d12">1778747345</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Primary Position" target="Engagement Area">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The primary position is oriented to cover an engagement area and prevent enemy penetration.</data>
  <data key="d9">defensive coverage,tactical planning</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d11">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1778747345</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Primary Position" target="Avenue of Approach">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The primary position covers the enemy's most likely avenue of approach.</data>
  <data key="d9">coverage,defensive strategy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d11">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1778747346</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alternate Position" target="Engagement Area">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alternate positions are located to allow occupants to continue covering the same engagement area if the primary position becomes unsuitable.</data>
  <data key="d9">continuity,tactical coverage</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7d8387d6c63026bf8e7495c788ece1b3</data>
  <data key="d11">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1778747346</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Supplementary Position" target="Avenue of Approach">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A supplementary position covers avenues of approach that are not the primary avenue, such as flanks.</data>
