<edge source="Soldier Lethality" target="United States Army">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship concerning Soldier Lethality and the United States Army is defined by the explicit recognition of Soldier Lethality as a vital aspect of force development. The United States Army lists Soldier Lethality as a core modernization priority, underscoring its centrality to current operational improvements. Furthermore, the United States Army designates Soldier Lethality as a key TACA Modernization Priority, integrating it into specific technical and acquisition frameworks aimed at enhancing combat effectiveness.

This prioritization extends beyond specific frameworks to encompass the entire organization. Soldier Lethality is identified as a key modernization priority within the United States Army enterprise, ensuring widespread adoption across departments. It is also formally listed as a modernization priority within the United States Army's strategic plan, aligning tactical capabilities with long-term strategic visions. Whether characterized as identified, designated, or core, the collective data confirms that Soldier Lethality is consistently maintained as a designated modernization priority for the United States Army.</data>
  <data key="d9">modernization,modernization focus,modernization goal,modernization priority,priority,strategic focus,strategic planning,strategic priority,strategy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-acade8ec9a9d5344060a4314cfa18a5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c4507fc3a4f571c8dfbaa23d9a738cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e07adaae816a485b8bdcdde27baecf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d02d8715ba139ee7e2b9f2ae7c7d9bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dcb0d8a5efb5ce308ca2c93988c72be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6faa94aab2e13591315f79ebbd49ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3473302fed80b78e94b810b62c26e3a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7ca33dacb79b2456dfa0debe68053e</data>
  <data key="d11">D:\Academic resources\WEAPON_SYSTEMS_HANDBOOK.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1778831772</data>
