<edge source="United States Army" target="Long-Range Precision Fires">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Long-Range Precision Fires constitutes a fundamental component of the strategic development and operational readiness plans maintained by the United States Army. Across various official designations and documentation, the United States Army lists Long-Range Precision Fires as a core modernization priority. This prioritization highlights the critical nature of the capability within the service branch's future force structure. Furthermore, the United States Army designates Long-Range Precision Fires as a key TACA Modernization Priority, linking it directly to specific transformation and acquisition authorities.

In terms of implementation and planning, Long-Range Precision Fires is recognized as a designated modernization priority within the Army's acquisition life cycle context. Additionally, the initiative is recorded as a modernization priority within the United States Army's strategic plan. Whether referenced as a key modernization priority or simply identified as a modernization priority for the United States Army, the descriptions uniformly affirm its status. Therefore, Long-Range Precision Fires serves as a designated modernization priority for the United States Army, reflecting a unified commitment to enhancing long-range strike capabilities through structured acquisition and strategic alignment.</data>
  <data key="d9">focus area,modernization,modernization focus,modernization goal,modernization priority,modernization strategy,priority,strategic focus,strategic priority,strategy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-acade8ec9a9d5344060a4314cfa18a5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c4507fc3a4f571c8dfbaa23d9a738cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e07adaae816a485b8bdcdde27baecf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d02d8715ba139ee7e2b9f2ae7c7d9bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dcb0d8a5efb5ce308ca2c93988c72be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3473302fed80b78e94b810b62c26e3a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15fb7baa23082d86c7d6fc25d3cc0e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7ca33dacb79b2456dfa0debe68053e</data>
  <data key="d11">D:\Academic resources\WEAPON_SYSTEMS_HANDBOOK.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1778831708</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="United States Army" target="Future Vertical Lift">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
